Short:        Converts raw binary into C source
Author:       Tyler Montbriand, AmigaOS 4.0 compile by Spot / Up Rough
Uploader:     Varthall / Up Rough <varti02 hotpop com>
Type:         dev/c
Architecture: ppc-amigaos >= 4.0.5

bindata

This program really IS stupidly simple. Feed it a filename and it converts the
raw binary contents of the file into a constant array in C source along with
it's length, to easily compile in tiny binary things into programs -- icons,
etc.

Update -- it works in Windows®, Solaris® SPARC, and AmigaOS 4.0 too.

Send comments, patches, ports etc to Tyler Montbriand, tsm()accesscomm.ca.